WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.028 --> 00:00:04.827
The seasons changed, and years passed.

2
00:00:04.828 --> 00:00:07.728
The four friends grew old.

3
00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:12.131
Rat and Mole rowed on the river less.

4
00:00:12.132 --> 00:00:16.312
Toad stayed indoors most days.

5
00:00:16.313 --> 00:00:19.545
Their neighbors wondered about them.

6
00:00:19.546 --> 00:00:24.279
"Have you seen Rat and Mole?" they asked.

7
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.110
"Do you know what Toad is doing?"

8
00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:33.708
But once in a while, the friends did go out.

9
00:00:33.709 --> 00:00:37.103
Then the Riverbankers noticed.

10
00:00:37.104 --> 00:00:40.857
When Toad went for a walk, they pointed.

11
00:00:40.858 --> 00:00:44.660
"There goes the modest Mr. Toad."

12
00:00:44.661 --> 00:00:48.709
"He is such a polite gentleman."

13
00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:54.021
When Rat and Mole went boating, young Riverbankers shouted:

14
00:00:54.022 --> 00:00:59.824
"Look! There's the great fighter, Water Rat!"

15
00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:06.892
The older ones said, "And there's good old Mole!"

16
00:01:06.893 --> 00:01:12.593
Toad, Rat, Mole, and Badger were famous.

17
00:01:12.594 --> 00:01:14.504
The reason was simple:

18
00:01:14.505 --> 00:01:18.421
Rat wrote a fine poem.

19
00:01:18.422 --> 00:01:23.966
It told the story of the great fight at Toad Hall.

20
00:01:23.967 --> 00:01:27.165
All the Riverbankers read it.

21
00:01:27.166 --> 00:01:30.493
Friends told the story to each other.

22
00:01:30.494 --> 00:01:34.498
Parents read the story to their children.

23
00:01:34.499 --> 00:01:38.874
Everyone told new tales about the friends.

24
00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:44.534
In these tales, Badger was always the scariest.

25
00:01:44.535 --> 00:01:48.235
"Badger is mean!" mothers told their children.

26
00:01:48.236 --> 00:01:51.163
"Be good or Badger will get you!"

27
00:01:51.164 --> 00:01:54.851
These stories about Badger were wrong.

28
00:01:54.852 --> 00:01:59.128
True, he didn't like crowds.

29
00:01:59.129 --> 00:02:03.403
But he loved children.

30
00:02:03.404 --> 00:02:09.326
The stories about the friends were told and retold.

31
00:02:09.327 --> 00:02:14.213
The tales became the music of the reeds.

32
00:02:14.214 --> 00:02:18.718
The poems became the song of the woods.

33
00:02:18.719 --> 00:02:27.214
And all became part of the wind in the willows.

